<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (We are establishing a 12-month price target for Coca-Cola of $76.77, which represents a 10% potential upside from the reference price 2. This valuation is the result of a comprehensive discounted cash flow \(DCF\) analysis that utilizes an EV/EBITDA exit multiple to determine the terminal value. We believe this hybrid methodology is the most appropriate for a company like Coca-Cola. The DCF component grounds the valuation in the company's fundamental ability to generate cash, while the use of a market-based exit multiple incorporates the market's current perception of the long-term value of similar stable, large-cap consumer staples companies.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
