/E (Rationale for Valuation Methodology)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( For a mature, predictable business like Coca-Cola, a DCF analysis is the preferred primary valuation tool as it focuses on the intrinsic value derived from future cash flows. Using an exit multiple instead of a perpetuity growth formula for the terminal value provides a crucial market-based check on the valuation. It helps capture the value of intangible assets like brand strength, which are reflected in the multiples that the market assigns to industry peers, while still being anchored to a five-year explicit forecast of fundamental performance.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
