/E (Weighted Average Cost of Capital \(WACC\): Our valuation employs a WACC of 6.03%. This was derived using the Capital Asset Pricing Model \(CAPM\). Key inputs to this calculation include a risk-free rate of 4.51%, a bottom-up beta of 0.57 \(reflecting the stock's low volatility relative to the broader market\), and a resulting cost of equity of 6.21% . The WACC reflects the blended cost of Coca-Cola's capital structure and serves as the discount rate for its future free cash flows.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 448 0 R
/E (Peer Selection & Exit Multiple: To determine an appropriate exit multiple, we selected a peer group of comparable large-cap beverage companies: PepsiCo, Keurig Dr. Pepper, and Monster Beverage. An analysis of the two-year forward EV/EBITDA multiples for this group yielded an average multiple of 14.97x . We applied this multiple to Coca-Cola's projected 2029 EBITDA to calculate its terminal value.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
